description:
What: Implement RemotePinClient that calls the IPFS Remote Pinning API (POST /pins, GET /pins/{requestid}, DELETE /pins/{requestid}) with timeout and Retry-After support.

Algorithm:
1. In crates/transit/src/retention/remote_pin_client.rs, add:

pub struct RemotePin { pub request_id: String, pub status: RemotePinStatus }
pub enum RemotePinStatus { Queued, Pinning, Pinned, Failed }

impl RemotePinStatus {
    pub fn is_terminal(&self) -> bool { matches!(self, Pinned | Failed) }
}

pub enum RemotePinError {
    Http(String),         -- network/HTTP error
    RateLimited(u64),     -- 429; contains Retry-After seconds
    ServiceError(u16, String),  -- 4xx/5xx with status code + body
    InvalidResponse(String),    -- unexpected response format
}

pub struct RemotePinClient {
    client: reqwest::Client,
    base_url: String,    -- e.g. https://api.pinata.cloud
    api_key: PinningApiKey,
}

impl RemotePinClient {
    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>, api_key: PinningApiKey, connect_timeout: Duration, request_timeout: Duration) -> Result<Self, String>
    -- builds reqwest::Client with both timeouts set

    pub async fn submit_pin(&self, cid: &str, name: &str) -> Result<RemotePin, RemotePinError>
    -- POST {base_url}/pins with JSON body {cid, name}
    -- Returns 202 with PinStatus JSON
    -- Handle 429: return RemotePinError::RateLimited(retry_after_secs)
    -- Handle 401: return RemotePinError::ServiceError(401, ...)
    -- Parse response JSON for requestid and status fields

    pub async fn check_status(&self, request_id: &str) -> Result<RemotePin, RemotePinError>
    -- GET {base_url}/pins/{request_id}
    -- Returns 200 with PinStatus JSON
    -- Handle 404: return RemotePinError::ServiceError(404, 'not found')
    -- Parse status field into RemotePinStatus

    pub async fn delete_pin(&self, request_id: &str) -> Result<(), RemotePinError>
    -- DELETE {base_url}/pins/{request_id}
    -- Returns 202; ignore body
}

2. JSON structures (use serde_json for deserialization):
   {"requestid": "...", "status": "queued|pinning|pinned|failed", "pin": {"cid": "...", "name": "..."}}

Defensive programming:
- Authorization header uses api_key.as_bearer_header() — NEVER log the header value
- Log only: status code, endpoint host, CID, request_id (all non-sensitive)
- Parse status field case-insensitively
- Set both connect_timeout AND total timeout on reqwest client
- On 429: parse Retry-After header (integer seconds or HTTP date); default to 60s if absent
- On unknown status string: treat as Pinning (safe conservative default)
